## Fix 1 (G1): undo the multi-repo clause added in 3ce83d0c6
In `internal/importer/importer.go` ~line 632 the condition is now `configuredPrefix != "" && config.GetMultiRepoConfig() == nil`. Remove the `&& config.GetMultiRepoConfig() == nil` part so the branch is selected by `configuredPrefix != ""` alone, exactly as commit 836ed2c07 had it. Reason, which the replacement comment must state plainly: `handleRename` creates the incoming id through `CreateIssue`, which validates it against the configured prefix regardless of multi-repo mode, so the configured-prefix test here is the same question that call will ask. Steering a foreign id past it (as 3ce83d0c6 did for multi-repo) reaches a create that cannot succeed and aborts the whole batch; the skip branch below is the only outcome that works, and its own comment already says so. Replace the four-line GH#686 comment with two or three lines saying that. If `config` is no longer used in this file after the change, remove the import.

## Fix 2 (G2): host env still masks two file-driven tests
In `internal/config/config_test.go`, `TestConfigFile` (~line 142) and `TestConfigPrecedence` (~line 198) write their own config file and `t.Chdir` into it, but viper ranks env above the file, so a host `BD_ACTOR=x`, `BD_JSON=true` or `BEADS_FLUSH_DEBOUNCE=99s` makes them fail. Split the env-clearing loop out of `isolateConfig` into its own helper (e.g. `clearBeadsEnv(t)`), have `isolateConfig` call it, and call it from those two tests before they `Initialize()`. No other behaviour change.

